.TH SAVE_WRITE 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
save_write \- Write size bytes of data to the slot file <dir>/<slot>.sav with a header carrying version
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqsave.h\(dq
.BI "bool save_write(const Save *s, const char *slot, const void *data, size_t size, uint32_t version);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write size bytes of data to the slot file <dir>/<slot>.sav with a header carrying version. data must be pointer\-free (a GameState): the bytes are written raw, so a pointer would be meaningless when read back. The normal call is save_write(&e\->save, "slot1", g, sizeof *g, SAVE_VERSION). Overwrites an existing slot. Fast enough to call on every checkpoint; a few hundred kilobytes is fine.
.SH RETURN VALUE
true on success; failures (unwritable folder, disk full) are logged.
.SH MODULE
save (src/engine/save/save.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR save_load (3),
.BR save_exists (3),
.BR save_delete (3),
.BR gge\-saves (7),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
